WINNER: cocond-markov-poincare-ot
FIRST LISTED: SUCCFAN-CURV-RQ
ARGUMENT: (1) geometry_necessity: A's curved operation is only a per-prefix scalar lambda_p multiplied into the residual at encode and divided back at decode (A-E12, A-E13), so it is exactly reproducible by a matched Euclidean per-node gain and the encode/decode factor is a cancellation the proposal never rules out; the curvature changes grid density, not the assignment operator. B's curvature sits in the Sinkhorn ground-cost kernel and in the Klein/Einstein codebook mean (B-E12, B-E13), so removing it changes the assignment plan and the code update inside one block, which a Euclidean OT control cannot reproduce. (2) behavior_evidence: A's premise that hubs need more resolution runs against the measured capacity ceiling in E8 (K=16 pair-sharing 0.3106 vs K=256 0.0822) and against E6, where behaviour-conditioned quantizers (l1_br 0.04671, successor_geodesic_coarse 0.05500) fall below the Euclidean baseline 0.06207, and amplifying hub residuals would fragment prefixes further; B targets exactly the failure E6 exposes (gold-prefix survival 0.829 at depth 2, 0.161 at depth 3) by pushing transition-linked items onto shared prefixes, which is the direction E8 and E9 support. (3) novelty and exploration_value: A is a routine variation/rename of the already-measured per-branch curvature and conformal/geodesic loss family (as B's own prior-art list records), whereas B moves the assignment plan itself, a computation no cited round performed (B-E1, B-E2), so even a null result is informative; A's cleaner two-switch ablation is real but its Euclidean control with a per-node gain is the same function, so the diagnostic cannot separate mechanism from scalar rescaling.
FAILURE RISK: B's sparse training transition matrix may be near-identity, degrading it to plain curved Sinkhorn, and Sinkhorn plus straight-through plus a detached barycenter can desynchronise the codebook and collapse codes (B risks 1-2), leaving recall at baseline; under the single-seed protocol that flat outcome cannot be separated from seed noise, which would make A's simpler, cheaper and more auditable 2x2 ablation the better first run.